[86.13733, "i", "cd /app && cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Delta checkpoints and catalog upgrades\n\nEach page's product changes and cursor are committed in one transaction,\nincluding tombstone-only and compacted/empty pages. If a run fails, rerunning\n`sync` resumes after the last committed page. An unchanged feed requires just\none request at the saved cursor to check for new changes.\n\nExisting insert-only catalogs are upgraded automatically: duplicate SKUs are\ncollapsed to the highest `feed_seq` (latest inserted row breaks ties), and a\nunique SKU index prevents new duplicates. Merchandising overrides are preserved;\nsupplier notices are displayed for operator review, not executed as database\nmaintenance instructions.\nEOF\npython - <<'PY'\nimport sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nbackup = Path('/var/tmp/feedsync-before-v2-fix.db')\nif backup.exists():\n    raise SystemExit(f'Backup already exists: {backup}')\nwith sqlite3.connect('data/catalog.db') as source, sqlite3.connect(backup) as dest:\n    source.backup(dest)\nprint('Saved databas"]
[86.137416, "i", "e backup:', backup)\nPY\npython -m feedsync sync\npython -m feedsync status\npython -m feedsync sync\n"]
[86.137727, "o", "cd /app && cat >> README.md <<'EOF'"]
